# Project Structure

```txt
src/
├── main.ts                         # Vite entry point
├── app/
│   ├── App.vue
│   ├── config/
│   │   ├── main.ts                 # Exports app-wide configuration
│   │   └── <config-name>/
│   │       ├── main.ts             # Required config entry point
│   │       └── ...                 # Config-only support files
│   └── layout/<layout-name>/       # App layouts and layout-only sections
├── shared/
│   ├── <system-name>/
│   │   ├── main.ts                 # Required public use-case entry point
│   │   ├── composable/             # Optional system-only support
│   │   ├── store/
│   │   ├── service/
│   │   └── ...
│   ├── component/                  # Global reusable UI
│   ├── i18n/ section/ lib/ asset/ composable/ store/ service/
│   └── ...                         # Optional global shared categories
└── feature/<feature-name>/
    ├── route.config.ts             # Required feature-owned route records
    ├── navigation.config.ts        # Required feature-owned menu entries
    ├── views/
    │   └── <view-name>/
    │       ├── main.vue            # Required route page entry
    │       ├── section/            # Optional view-only sections
    │       ├── i18n/ lib/ asset/ composable/ store/ service/
    │       └── ...                 # Other view-only support files
    ├── component/ i18n/ section/ lib/ asset/ composable/ store/ service/
    └── ...                         # Optional feature-wide support
```

## Ownership and imports

- `shared` code is available to both `app` and every feature. Shared code may depend only on shared code and external libraries.
- A feature may depend on its own feature and shared; cross-feature and feature-to-app imports are forbidden.
- The app layer owns application setup and composes feature route/navigation configs with app layouts.
- Keep support code at the narrowest scope that uses it: a view, a feature, a shared system, or global shared.
- Shared systems expose supported use cases from their `main.ts`; system-only support files stay inside that system.

## Layout, view, section, component

- App layouts live in `src/app/layout/<layout-name>/`.
- Feature route pages live in `src/feature/<feature>/views/<view>/main.vue`.
- View-only sections live under that view's `section/`; layout-only sections stay with their layout.
- Reusable UI belongs to the feature's `component/` or global `src/shared/component/`, based on consumers.

